The `tokenizerId` property.

In the test ("records the injected tokenizer id on every outcome so swapping tokenizers is a deliberate diff rather than a silent shift of every recorded range (§17)"), the simulator built with the byte tokenizer asserts:

```ts
const bytes = new ProviderCacheSimulator({
  tokenizer: new ExactTokenizer('bytes-v0', (text) => text.length),
}).submit(prompt);

expect(bytes.tokenizerId).toBe('bytes-v0');
```

So the expected value of `'bytes-v0'` is on `bytes.tokenizerId` — the simulator records the injected tokenizer's id on the outcome so that swapping tokenizers shows up as a deliberate, visible diff rather than silently shifting every recorded token range.
